              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
            evaluate <math id="alg1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> via (<a href="#S5.E16" title="In V-D RRT-Guided Local Replanning with STL Awareness ‣ V E2E Structural Moe Model ‣ Bridging Perception and Planning: Towards End-to-End Planningfor Signal Temporal Logic Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) and update the incumbent best
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
            <math id="alg1.m32" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{Y}}_{\tau:\tau+H}\leftarrow\texttt{best\_path}(\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">best_path</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{Y}}_{\tau:\tau+H}\leftarrow\texttt{best\_path}(\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg1.5.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">smooth<math id="alg1.m33" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\tilde{\mathbf{Y}}_{\tau:\tau+H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mathbf{Y}}_{\tau:\tau+H})</annotation></semantics></math></span>;
<math id="alg1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow\tau+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow\tau+1</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg1.5.17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">continue</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16</span></span>
            <math id="alg1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.5.19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.5.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17</span></span>
            Return repaired <math id="alg1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">V-D</span> </span><span id="S5.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">RRT-Guided Local Replanning with STL Awareness</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a nominal trajectory <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{Y}}=\{(x_{t},y_{t},\theta_{t})\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{Y}}=\{(x_{t},y_{t},\theta_{t})\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we run a rollout-and-check loop.
If a forward lookahead at time <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> indicates (i) collision/kinematic violation, or (ii) <em id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">STL robustness</em>
of the local window is negative, we trigger short-horizon RRT-style replanning on <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tau,\tau{+}H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tau,\tau{+}H]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Expansion is goal-biased: with probability <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> targets are sampled near nominal anchors
<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{p}_{t}\}_{t=\tau}^{\tau+H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{p}_{t}\}_{t=\tau}^{\tau+H}</annotation></semantics></math>,
otherwise uniformly. Candidate edges must satisfy local limits
<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{t}-p_{t-1}\|\!\leq\!d_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{t}-p_{t-1}\|\!\leq\!d_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\theta_{t}-\theta_{t-1}|\!\leq\!\Delta\theta_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\theta_{t}-\theta_{t-1}|\!\leq\!\Delta\theta_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Among feasible branches that reach <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau{+}H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau{+}H</annotation></semantics></math>, we select the path minimizing</p>
<table id="S5.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{J}=\sum_{t=\tau}^{\tau+H}\!\Big(\lambda_{1}\|p_{t}-\hat{p}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda_{2}\,\kappa_{t}^{2}\Big)\;-\;\lambda_{3}\,\tilde{\rho}_{\varphi}\!\big(\mathbf{Y}_{\tau:\tau+H}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>φ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}=\sum_{t=\tau}^{\tau+H}\!\Big(\lambda_{1}\|p_{t}-\hat{p}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda_{2}\,\kappa_{t}^{2}\Big)\;-\;\lambda_{3}\,\tilde{\rho}_{\varphi}\!\big(\mathbf{Y}_{\tau:\tau+H}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}=(x_{t},y_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}=(x_{t},y_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a discrete curvature proxy, and <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\rho}_{\varphi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>φ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\rho}_{\varphi}</annotation></semantics></math> is a (smoothed)
STL robustness of the segment (higher is better). The repaired segment is optionally smoothed (e.g., cubic spline)
and spliced back into <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The full procedures, termed <span id="S5.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TSP</span>, is shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In V-C Training Objective ‣ V E2E Structural Moe Model ‣ Bridging Perception and Planning: Towards End-to-End Planningfor Signal Temporal Logic Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
